        "9": {
          "id": "9",
          "name": "data.js",
          "contents": "const contributors = [\n  {\n    id: 'turing',\n    name: 'Alan Turing',\n    initials: 'AT',\n    color: '#4F46E5',\n    label: 'Foundational Questions',\n    what: \"Turing was a mathematician and computer scientist who helped give machine intelligence one of its earliest and most important questions: <em>Can machines think?</em> In a 1950 paper, he proposed the imitation game — now called the Turing Test — as a way to evaluate whether a machine could produce responses indistinguishable from a human.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Alan-Turing' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Turing's ideas belong to the earliest stage of AI history, before the field even had a name. He connected mathematics, computing, and philosophy of mind in ways that gave future researchers a framework for thinking about machine intelligence.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Alan-Turing' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"By asking a practical question instead of a purely philosophical one, Turing made the study of machine intelligence something researchers could actually investigate. The Turing Test is still debated today as AI systems become capable of generating increasingly fluent, human-like responses.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Alan-Turing' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup><sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.history.com/articles/alan-turing' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'Britannica — Alan Turing', url: 'https://www.britannica.com/biography/Alan-Turing' },\n      { label: 'HISTORY — Alan Turing', url: 'https://www.history.com/articles/alan-turing' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'mccarthy',\n    name: 'John McCarthy',\n    initials: 'JM',\n    color: '#0369A1',\n    label: 'Named and Founded the Field',\n    what: \"McCarthy was a computer scientist who helped establish AI as a formal discipline. In 1955, he coined the term &ldquo;artificial intelligence&rdquo; and helped organize the 1956 Dartmouth Conference — the workshop widely treated as the founding moment of AI as a field.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://dartmouthalumnimagazine.com/articles/birth-artificial-intelligence' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup> He also created LISP, a programming language designed for symbolic AI research.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"McCarthy’s contributions sit at the very beginning of AI as a recognized discipline. By naming the field and convening its first major research gathering, he turned a collection of ideas into an organized scientific effort with a shared identity and agenda.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"Without a name and a community, AI might have developed more slowly or in a fragmented way. McCarthy’s role in naming, organizing, and building tools for the field helped researchers collaborate and build on each other's work from the very start.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'Computer History Museum — John McCarthy', url: 'https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy' },\n      { label: 'Dartmouth Alumni Magazine — The Birth of Artificial Intelligence', url: 'https://dartmouthalumnimagazine.com/articles/birth-artificial-intelligence' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'minsky',\n    name: 'Marvin Minsky',\n    initials: 'MM',\n    color: '#047857',\n    label: 'AI Pioneer & Theorist',\n    what: \"Minsky was a mathematician and cognitive scientist who cofounded the MIT Artificial Intelligence Laboratory with John McCarthy in 1959. He worked on early neural networks, robotics, and theories about how both machines and humans represent knowledge.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/marvin-minsky' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Minsky’s work spans the early symbolic AI era. His ideas about knowledge representation — including &ldquo;frames,&rdquo; a structured way of organizing information — shaped how early AI systems were designed to understand and reason about the world.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/marvin-minsky' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup><sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Marvin-Minsky' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"By connecting AI to questions about how minds work, Minsky helped establish cognitive science alongside computer science as a companion field. The MIT AI Lab he cofounded became one of the most important centers of AI research in the world for decades.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://computerhistory.org/profile/marvin-minsky' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'Computer History Museum — Marvin Minsky', url: 'https://computerhistory.org/profile/marvin-minsky' },\n      { label: 'Britannica — Marvin Minsky', url: 'https://www.britannica.com/biography/Marvin-Minsky' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'hopper',\n    name: 'Grace Hopper',\n    initials: 'GH',\n    color: '#B45309',\n    label: 'Programming Language Pioneer',\n    what: \"Hopper was a mathematician and Navy officer who became one of the most important figures in the history of programming. She helped develop one of the first compilers — programs that translate human-readable code into machine instructions — and was a driving force behind COBOL, a widely used business programming language.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.womenshistory.org/education-resources/biographies/grace-hopper' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Hopper’s contributions belong to the computing foundations that made AI possible. Before compilers and higher-level languages, programming required working directly in machine code — a barrier that limited who could use computers and what they could do.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Grace-Hopper' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"By advocating for word-based programming languages, Hopper helped make computers usable by far more people. Her work opened computing — and eventually AI — to developers who were not specialists in machine-level code, expanding who could participate in building these technologies.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.womenshistory.org/education-resources/biographies/grace-hopper' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: \"National Women’s History Museum — Grace Hopper\", url: 'https://www.womenshistory.org/education-resources/biographies/grace-hopper' },\n      { label: 'Britannica — Grace Hopper', url: 'https://www.britannica.com/biography/Grace-Hopper' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'li',\n    name: 'Fei-Fei Li',\n    initials: 'FL',\n    color: '#7C3AED',\n    label: 'ImageNet & Computer Vision',\n    what: \"Li is a computer scientist and AI researcher who led the creation of ImageNet, a dataset of millions of labeled images. The annual ImageNet competition challenged AI systems to correctly classify images from this massive dataset — and helped drive major breakthroughs in computer vision and deep learning in the 2010s.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Fei-Fei-Li' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Li’s work connects to the deep learning era of AI history. The ImageNet competition results showed that large neural networks trained on huge labeled datasets could dramatically outperform older approaches — a shift that accelerated the modern wave of AI development.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.ted.com/talks/fei_fei_li_how_we_re_teaching_computers_to_understand_pictures' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"ImageNet demonstrated that the quality and scale of training data could be just as important as the algorithm itself. Li’s work helped establish data curation and large-scale benchmarks as essential tools for AI — an insight that continues to shape how AI systems are built today.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.britannica.com/biography/Fei-Fei-Li' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'Britannica — Fei-Fei Li', url: 'https://www.britannica.com/biography/Fei-Fei-Li' },\n      { label: \"TED — How we’re teaching computers to understand pictures\", url: 'https://www.ted.com/talks/fei_fei_li_how_we_re_teaching_computers_to_understand_pictures' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'buolamwini',\n    name: 'Joy Buolamwini',\n    initials: 'JB',\n    color: '#BE185D',\n    label: 'Algorithmic Justice',\n    what: \"Buolamwini is a computer scientist and founder of the Algorithmic Justice League. While a student at MIT, she discovered that commercial facial analysis software performed significantly worse on darker-skinned and women’s faces. Her Gender Shades research documented these disparities in AI systems from major technology companies.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.ted.com/talks/joy_buolamwini_how_i_m_fighting_bias_in_algorithms' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Buolamwini’s work belongs to the emerging field of AI ethics and accountability. It showed that AI systems can reflect and amplify bias from the data they are trained on — and that testing on non-representative samples can hide serious failures.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://news.mit.edu/2018/study-finds-gender-skin-type-bias-artificial-intelligence-systems-0212' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"By documenting that commercial AI systems performed unevenly across different groups, Buolamwini helped push algorithmic fairness into public and policy debate. Her advocacy contributed to legislative efforts around facial recognition regulation and pressure on companies to improve their testing practices.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.ted.com/talks/joy_buolamwini_how_i_m_fighting_bias_in_algorithms' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: \"TED — How I’m fighting bias in algorithms\", url: 'https://www.ted.com/talks/joy_buolamwini_how_i_m_fighting_bias_in_algorithms' },\n      { label: 'MIT News — Study finds gender and skin-type bias in AI systems', url: 'https://news.mit.edu/2018/study-finds-gender-skin-type-bias-artificial-intelligence-systems-0212' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'gebru',\n    name: 'Timnit Gebru',\n    initials: 'TG',\n    color: '#B91C1C',\n    label: 'AI Ethics & Accountability',\n    what: \"Gebru is a computer scientist and AI ethics researcher who co-authored the Gender Shades study on facial recognition bias, and later co-wrote an influential paper on the risks of large language models. After a high-profile departure from Google in 2020, she founded the Distributed AI Research Institute (DAIR) to support independent AI research.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://time.com/collections/time100-ai/6308988/timnit-gebru-ai/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Gebru’s work connects to growing debates about AI accountability, especially as large-scale AI systems became more commercially significant. Her research showed that bias in facial recognition and risks from language models were not just technical problems — they were social and ethical ones.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://news.mit.edu/2018/study-finds-gender-skin-type-bias-artificial-intelligence-systems-0212' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"Gebru’s career illustrates both the importance and the difficulty of doing critical AI research inside and outside large technology companies. Her work helped establish AI ethics as a serious field of inquiry and pushed the industry to reckon with the social consequences of large AI systems.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://time.com/collections/time100-ai/6308988/timnit-gebru-ai/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'TIME100 AI — Timnit Gebru', url: 'https://time.com/collections/time100-ai/6308988/timnit-gebru-ai/' },\n      { label: 'MIT News — Study finds gender and skin-type bias in AI systems', url: 'https://news.mit.edu/2018/study-finds-gender-skin-type-bias-artificial-intelligence-systems-0212' }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'benjamin',\n    name: 'Ruha Benjamin',\n    initials: 'RB',\n    color: '#0F766E',\n    label: 'Technology & Social Justice',\n    what: \"Benjamin is a scholar of science, technology, and society whose work examines how technologies — including AI — can appear neutral while reinforcing existing inequalities. Her book <em>Race After Technology</em> introduced the concept of the &ldquo;New Jim Code&rdquo; to describe how discriminatory practices can be embedded in digital tools and algorithms.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.macfound.org/fellows/class-of-2024/ruha-benjamin' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    era: \"Benjamin’s contributions belong to the critical study of AI’s social impact. Her work connects AI bias to broader histories of race, inequality, and institutional design — pushing researchers to ask not just whether a system is accurate, but who it serves and who it may harm.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.ias.edu/ideas/race-after-technology' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>2</a></sup>\",\n    why: \"By bringing social science and humanities perspectives to AI, Benjamin helps explain why technical accuracy alone is not enough to make a system fair. Her scholarship pushes researchers, designers, and policymakers to examine whose interests AI systems are built to serve.<sup class='fn'><a href='https://www.macfound.org/fellows/class-of-2024/ruha-benjamin' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>1</a></sup>\",\n    sources: [\n      { label: 'MacArthur Foundation — Ruha Benjamin', url: 'https://www.macfound.org/fellows/class-of-2024/ruha-benjamin' },\n      { label: 'Institute for Advanced Study — Race After Technology', url: 'https://www.ias.edu/ideas/race-after-technology' }\n    ]\n  }\n];\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "12": {
          "id": "12",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "function renderGrid() {\n  var grid = document.getElementById('contributorGrid');\n  grid.innerHTML = '';\n  for (var i = 0; i < contributors.length; i++) {\n    var c = contributors[i];\n    var card = document.createElement('div');\n    card.className = 'contributor-card';\n    card.setAttribute('data-id', c.id);\n    card.innerHTML =\n      '<img class=\"card-photo\" src=\"images/' + c.id + '.jpg\" alt=\"' + c.name + '\">' +\n      '<div class=\"card-info\">' +\n        '<div class=\"card-name\">' + c.name + '</div>' +\n        '<div class=\"card-label\">' + c.label + '</div>' +\n      '</div>';\n    card.addEventListener('click', (function(id) {\n      return function() { showProfile(id); };\n    })(c.id));\n    grid.appendChild(card);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction showProfile(id) {\n  var c = null;\n  for (var i = 0; i < contributors.length; i++) {\n    if (contributors[i].id === id) { c = contributors[i]; break; }\n  }\n  if (!c) return;\n\n  var sourcesHtml = '';\n  for (var s = 0; s < c.sources.length; s++) {\n    sourcesHtml +=\n      '<li><a href=\"' + c.sources[s].url + '\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">' +\n      c.sources[s].label + '</a></li>';\n  }\n\n  var profile = document.getElementById('profileView');\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-photo').src = 'images/' + c.id + '.jpg';\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-photo').alt = c.name;\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-name').textContent = c.name;\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-label').textContent = c.label;\n  profile.querySelector('.section-what .section-body').innerHTML = c.what;\n  profile.querySelector('.section-era .section-body').innerHTML = c.era;\n  profile.querySelector('.section-why .section-body').innerHTML = c.why;\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-sources ol').innerHTML = sourcesHtml;\n  profile.querySelector('.profile-sources').removeAttribute('open');\n\n  document.getElementById('gridView').style.display = 'none';\n  profile.style.display = 'block';\n  window.scrollTo(0, 0);\n}\n\nfunction showGrid() {\n  document.getElementById('profileView').style.display = 'none';\n  document.getElementById('gridView').style.display = 'block';\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById('backBtn').addEventListener('click', showGrid);\n\nrenderGrid();\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "13": {
          "id": "13",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "/* ── Reset & Base ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n\n:root {\n  --bg:           #F7F8FC;\n  --card-bg:      #FFFFFF;\n  --text:         #1A1A2E;\n  --text-muted:   #6B7280;\n  --border:       #E5E7EB;\n  --accent:       #2563EB;\n  --radius-sm:    6px;\n  --radius-md:    12px;\n  --radius-lg:    16px;\n  --shadow:       0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.07), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n  --shadow-hover: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.13);\n  --transition:   0.18s ease;\n}\n\nbody {\n  font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n}\n\n/* ── Header ───────────────────────────────────────────── */\n.page-header {\n  background: #1A1A2E;\n  color: white;\n  padding: 20px 24px 16px;\n}\n\n.page-header h1 {\n  font-size: 1.4rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n\n.header-sub {\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.48);\n}\n\n/* ── Grid view ────────────────────────────────────────── */\n#gridView {\n  padding: 20px 20px 32px;\n}\n\n.contributor-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n/* ── Contributor card ─────────────────────────────────── */\n.contributor-card {\n  background: var(--card-bg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n  overflow: hidden;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: box-shadow var(--transition), transform var(--transition);\n}\n\n.contributor-card:hover {\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-hover);\n  transform: translateY(-2px);\n}\n\n.card-photo {\n  width: 100%;\n  aspect-ratio: 1;\n  object-fit: cover;\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.card-info {\n  padding: 8px 8px 10px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\n.card-name {\n  font-size: 0.76rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  color: var(--text);\n  line-height: 1.3;\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n\n.card-label {\n  font-size: 0.63rem;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  line-height: 1.3;\n}\n\n/* ── Profile view ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n#profileView {\n  padding-bottom: 32px;\n}\n\n.profile-back-bar {\n  padding: 14px 20px 4px;\n}\n\n.back-btn {\n  background: none;\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  font-size: 0.82rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  padding: 6px 14px;\n  border-radius: 20px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: all var(--transition);\n  font-family: inherit;\n}\n\n.back-btn:hover {\n  background: var(--card-bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  border-color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n.profile-card {\n  margin: 12px 20px 0;\n  background: var(--card-bg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow);\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.profile-photo-area {\n  padding: 28px 24px 0;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.profile-photo {\n  width: 108px;\n  height: 108px;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  object-fit: cover;\n  display: block;\n}\n\n.profile-content {\n  padding: 18px 24px 24px;\n}\n\n.profile-name {\n  font-size: 1.45rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n  text-align: center;\n  margin-bottom: 6px;\n}\n\n.profile-label {\n  display: block;\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 0.7rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  margin-bottom: 22px;\n}\n\n/* ── Profile sections ─────────────────────────────────── */\n.profile-section {\n  margin-bottom: 18px;\n  padding-bottom: 18px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.profile-section:last-of-type {\n  border-bottom: none;\n  margin-bottom: 0;\n  padding-bottom: 0;\n}\n\n.section-heading {\n  font-size: 0.67rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.section-body {\n  font-size: 0.875rem;\n  line-height: 1.75;\n  color: var(--text);\n}\n\n/* ── Footnote links ───────────────────────────────────── */\nsup.fn {\n  font-size: 0.65em;\n  line-height: 0;\n  vertical-align: super;\n  margin-left: 1px;\n}\n\nsup.fn a {\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--text-muted);\n  padding: 0 1px;\n}\n\nsup.fn a:hover {\n  color: var(--text);\n  border-bottom-color: var(--text);\n}\n\n/* ── Sources (collapsible) ────────────────────────────── */\n.profile-sources {\n  margin-top: 20px;\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.profile-sources .sources-label {\n  font-size: 0.67rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.07em;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  user-select: none;\n  list-style: none;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 4px;\n}\n\n.profile-sources .sources-label::before {\n  content: '▶';\n  font-size: 0.55rem;\n  transition: transform var(--transition);\n}\n\n.profile-sources[open] .sources-label::before {\n  transform: rotate(90deg);\n}\n\n.profile-sources ol {\n  margin: 8px 0 2px;\n  padding-left: 18px;\n}\n\n.profile-sources li {\n  font-size: 0.78rem;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  margin-bottom: 2px;\n}\n\n.profile-sources a {\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.profile-sources a:hover {\n  color: var(--text);\n  border-bottom-color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* ── Footer & photo credits ───────────────────────────── */\n.page-footer {\n  padding: 12px 20px 20px;\n}\n\n.photo-credits {\n  padding: 8px 14px;\n  background: var(--card-bg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n\n.credits-label {\n  font-size: 0.67rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.07em;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  user-select: none;\n  list-style: none;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 4px;\n}\n\n.credits-label::before {\n  content: '▶';\n  font-size: 0.55rem;\n  transition: transform var(--transition);\n}\n\n.photo-credits[open] .credits-label::before {\n  transform: rotate(90deg);\n}\n\n.photo-credits ul {\n  margin: 8px 0 2px;\n  padding-left: 18px;\n}\n\n.photo-credits li {\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n  color: var(--text-muted);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n/* ── Responsive ───────────────────────────────────────── */\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  .contributor-grid  { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }\n  .page-header h1    { font-size: 1.2rem; }\n  .profile-card      { margin: 12px 14px 0; }\n  .profile-content   { padding: 16px 18px 20px; }\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "14": {
          "id": "14",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>People Who Shaped AI</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <header class=\"page-header\">\n    <h1>People Who Shaped AI</h1>\n    <p class=\"header-sub\">Select a contributor to explore their work</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <!-- Grid view -->\n  <div id=\"gridView\">\n    <div id=\"contributorGrid\" class=\"contributor-grid\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Profile view (hidden until a card is clicked) -->\n  <div id=\"profileView\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <div class=\"profile-back-bar\">\n      <button id=\"backBtn\" class=\"back-btn\">&#8592; Back to contributors</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"profile-card\">\n      <div class=\"profile-photo-area\">\n        <img class=\"profile-photo\" src=\"\" alt=\"\">\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"profile-content\">\n        <h2 class=\"profile-name\"></h2>\n        <span class=\"profile-label\"></span>\n\n        <div class=\"profile-section section-what\">\n          <div class=\"section-heading\">What did they contribute?</div>\n          <div class=\"section-body\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"profile-section section-era\">\n          <div class=\"section-heading\">What part of AI history does this connect to?</div>\n          <div class=\"section-body\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"profile-section section-why\">\n          <div class=\"section-heading\">Why does this contribution matter?</div>\n          <div class=\"section-body\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <details class=\"profile-sources\">\n          <summary class=\"sources-label\">Sources</summary>\n          <ol></ol>\n        </details>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <footer class=\"page-footer\">\n    <details class=\"photo-credits\">\n      <summary class=\"credits-label\">Photo credits</summary>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Alan Turing &mdash; Elliott &amp; Fry, 1951. Public domain.</li>\n        <li>John McCarthy &mdash; &ldquo;null0,&rdquo; 2006. CC BY-SA 2.0.</li>\n        <li>Marvin Minsky &mdash; Sethwoodworth, 2008. CC BY 3.0.</li>\n        <li>Grace Hopper &mdash; James S. Davis, 1984. Public domain.</li>\n        <li>Fei-Fei Li &mdash; ITU Pictures, 2017. CC BY 2.0.</li>\n        <li>Joy Buolamwini &mdash; Niccol&ograve; Caranti, 2018. CC BY-SA 4.0.</li>\n        <li>Timnit Gebru &mdash; Kimberly White / TechCrunch, 2018. CC BY 2.0.</li>\n        <li>Ruha Benjamin &mdash; Data &amp; Society Research Institute, 2019. CC BY 3.0.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </details>\n  </footer>\n\n  <script src=\"data.js\"></script>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "13",
        "14"
      ]
    },
